{"hero|A bent support strut from the ceiling. Heavy, sturdy, and very pry-ish.":"1eeefb8aa89e","hero|KIT MARLOW, ENGINEER 2ND CLASS. The photo makes me look like I already knew this would happen.":"fb9af320ad47","hero|Insulated work gloves, rated to twenty thousand volts. Rated zero for style.":"e48ce07b3209","hero|A fire extinguisher. Fully charged. Unlike me.":"a04f56df0389","hero|KIT MARLOW. YARD ENGINEERING. CLEARANCE 1. The photo was taken before I'd had coffee, and it shows.":"da6a201bd016","hero|My trusty multitool. Wrench, driver, pliers, and a bottle opener I have never used on shift. Officially.":"7d87f8e609d2","hero|Black coffee. Ninety-two degrees, according to the machine. Hot enough to make steel expand. A tiny bit.":"7b29719d5999","hero|A heavy wrench. In zero-g it's also a perfectly good thruster. Just throw it.":"b10709b9c165","hero|A long, heavy-gauge power cable. Dead now that I yanked it out of the ceiling. Probably.":"6a3882da7941","hero|My bunk. Still warm.":"6850f15ff2d5","hero|Unlike space.":"f94e956b7c34","hero|No time for a nap. Even though I REALLY want one.":"e699822c33c7","hero|It's bolted down. Everything's bolted down. Except, apparently, the ceiling.":"518eda09e279","hero|The drawers are just full of socks. Lucky socks, but socks.":"155de1813edf","hero|\"SAFETY FIRST.\" Everyone else is gone, so I guess safety is my job now.":"a36efacc06f1","hero|I'll leave it for the next crew. If there IS a next crew.":"65d027e053ad","hero|The vent is coughing up smoke. That's the exact opposite of what vents are for.":"aeebe65f100e","hero|I'm not crawling into a smoking vent. I've seen those movies.":"79d99a7e8c26","hero|That's Ares Prime down there. Red dust, thin air, one tiny colony...":"9d51771cfa5c","hero|...and in about twenty minutes, this ship becomes its newest meteor shower.":"648c0efb95e4","hero|Opening a window in orbit. Bold. Fatal, but bold.":"7ac302d21214","hero|My desk. A photo of Mom, cold coffee, and maintenance reports nobody read.":"1cf3caf458ba","hero|Every report says 'CRITICAL'. Every one is stamped 'IGNORED'.":"20866f5aeea0","hero|I'm not carrying a desk to the pod.":"f11906b67cb3","hero|Mom. She told me to take the desk job planetside. I'll never hear the end of this.":"84bf9f48345f","hero|I'll come back for her. The photo, I mean. Mom's on the planet. Which is where I'm going.":"06a2f2cad2c9","hero|The screen just flashes 'ABANDON SHIP' over and over. Very supportive.":"e93680a2fed3","hero|It's frozen. Like my career prospects.":"bc5e8f414082","hero|My ID card. Pretty sure the pod bay will want to see it.":"1a441e0dc186","hero|My ID card. Never leave home without it.":"1130496314f2","hero|Especially when home is exploding.":"ae4588315d14","hero|My locker. Smells like old boots and regret.":"6c3852fb8e82","hero|My locker. My emergency gear's in there.":"3c627a956367","hero|It's already open.":"f394e86f7f18","hero|Aha! My insulated work gloves.":"c011d398edd1","hero|It's bolted to the wall.":"4306afa46f53","hero|My insulated gloves. Rated for twenty thousand volts.":"87664fecedda","hero|Got the gloves. Snug, and very non-conductive.":"ae9f889a77dc","hero|Exposed wiring. The ship's nervous system is having a breakdown. Relatable.":"5a3c110b6a6e","hero|Not with my bare hands.":"a4baaccd8586","hero|It's still connected to the ship. And to a LOT of volts.":"b72f5733709e","hero|Gloves or not, ripping out random wiring won't help. Probably.":"63ff22cd83c0","hero|Just crumbled ceiling bits now.":"06ca989c4478","hero|A chunk of the ceiling came down. There's a sturdy metal strut sticking out of it.":"e12a003dedb7","hero|The rest is just crumbly junk.":"fdc0e7f7f367","hero|A metal strut. Perfect for prying things.":"5f0a98b24cc4","hero|Or for dramatic gestures.":"51dc45bbe95f","hero|The ceiling lamp is hanging by its wires and spitting sparks. Mood lighting.":"5bb0bf9b1b4a","hero|It's hanging from live wires. I'll pass.":"c26a3be48dfb","hero|It's already doing all it can.":"9b04007a7af8","hero|Pried open. Freedom smells like burning insulation.":"4e60890fd497","hero|The door to the corridor. Normally it goes 'swoosh'. Now it just sits there.":"2a95feb95b65","hero|It's jammed. The door servos are dead.":"12885a12e574","hero|If only I had something to pry it open with...":"113eaccade82","hero|I push the button. Nothing. The servos are fried.":"13ca15a25a91","hero|Hnnnngh...":"994d228933de","hero|GOT it!":"72476436decf","hero|It's a jammed door, not a locked one. Swiping won't help.":"a09ea33f4485","hero|Back to my quarters. Nothing left there but socks.":"a1d8e1c2bd15","hero|The hatch to the cargo hold. A ladder leads down into the dark.":"9900e79b90d8","hero|A floor hatch down to the cargo hold.":"0b6313f763ce","hero|Pry against six tonnes of air pressure? Physics says no.":"727950617e28","hero|Physics says it LOUDLY.":"a940ba9b7c54","hero|It's a hatch, not a vending machine.":"ce37b8051065","hero|CORRIDOR: 1.0 ATM. HOLD: 1.0 ATM. Balanced. Like a well-adjusted person.":"800884c8fbf9","hero|CORRIDOR: 1.0 ATM. HOLD: 0.4 ATM.":"a2280132f669","hero|The cargo hold's been leaking air. That's a big pressure difference.":"5b6472578282","hero|A pressure equalization valve. It connects the corridor air to the cargo hold.":"f7527392d624","hero|It's plumbed in. Turning it is more my speed.":"29a87c72661b","hero|MABEL, the ship's AI. 'Maintenance And Basic Electronic Logistics.' She hates being called Mabes.":"84c4ab5cafc9","hero|She's built into the wall. Also, rude.":"24f0bc85c15d","hero|Engineering. The door's stuck halfway and there's smoke pouring out. Probably fine.":"92d641e87f5f","hero|It's stuck halfway, but I can squeeze through.":"4bf9379cf4f2","hero|Bits of hull are peeling off and drifting away. My ship is leaving without me. In pieces.":"c9f212d74fd3","hero|An empty case and a lot of broken glass.":"c5ef369244db","hero|The extinguisher is just sitting there, waiting for me.":"3e2f477a0325","hero|\"IN CASE OF FIRE, BREAK GLASS.\" Well, there's PLENTY of fire.":"d3ba0991cbc7","hero|It's about as open as it gets now.":"73ad5159014a","hero|It's locked. Somebody took 'break glass' very literally.":"0144d4a3e021","hero|I already took it.":"7cc3210b8f1c","hero|It's behind glass. Locked glass. Very sturdy-looking... glass.":"6332fe7abc80","hero|One fire extinguisher, coming with me.":"ea9910441e36","hero|I'd rather just take the extinguisher.":"e1be31b4cf3b","hero|I'd need something solid to break the glass.":"1445019d9dae","hero|It's already smashed.":"9ad0df2d10f6","hero|In case of fire: break glass.":"17bf9b766eee","hero|Done and done.":"7f5d736f3259","hero|This is an emergency, not a library.":"5614d6af885e","hero|The escape pod bay! And a live cable thrashing around right in front of it.":"09529390575c","hero|The pod bay. My ride is waiting.":"423ec7973afd","hero|The pod bay door. Sealed tight.":"4b2b6fe26957","hero|Not with that live cable whipping around. I like my eyebrows where they are.":"189c5037fcfc","hero|No power. The door panel is completely dead.":"fc626dc1ef88","hero|It's locked. The panel next to it wants an ID card.":"3a9f87114e04","hero|There's a panel right beside it for that.":"42604a801ae7","hero|This door is thicker than my skull. And that's saying something.":"8dcd8d34c7f7","hero|The door panel. Dark. No power at all.":"c8a0ec2b8958","hero|Green light. Sweet, sweet green light.":"3ddbbb05f5ea","hero|It's got power now! It's asking for an ID card.":"4c0d06fe0fa3","hero|I can't reach it with that cable thrashing around.":"1aaf515d8909","hero|I poke the buttons. Nothing. Dead as a doornail.":"efcdab0a28ad","hero|ID CARD REQUIRED, it says. Of course it does.":"1414bc07499c","hero|A severed power cable, thrashing around and spitting sparks. It's blocking the pod bay door.":"d05017aedde0","hero|Grab a live cable with my bare hands?":"5da8393f3079","hero|I'd like to keep my skeleton on the inside.":"0864dd0f8ec5","hero|Poke a live wire with a metal stick? Great plan. Very final.":"d08d33d8066b","hero|Spray a live wire? That's how you become a cautionary tale in the safety manual.":"1fe697b83dd6","hero|It doesn't care who I am.":"f09004ac7444","hero|Whoa. The whole corridor is falling apart.":"4a0f4ce9edcf","hero|The escape pods are past that door. Past that very angry cable.":"78b3cd990fb4","hero|Back to the corridor.":"915a9fc78e6c","hero|The main engineering console. Mostly red lights. Plus some angrier red lights.":"08b3d3f7ee90","hero|The reactor core. It's supposed to be a calm blue.":"232b489b465b","hero|It is not a calm blue.":"0ce1c4399516","hero|I'm an engineer, not a miracle worker. That core is done.":"3aaf4edc216b","hero|Sure. I'll just pop it in my pocket.":"36a957a0c593","hero|Please don't explode please don't explode please don't explode.":"6718abfc590a","hero|That's a fusion reaction. It laughs at fire extinguishers.":"084bac492069","hero|A cracked coolant pipe, venting steam. The valve's rusted solid.":"3173e1ce041c","hero|It won't budge. Not that it'd help now.":"a964ff5b4c0f","hero|Even with the strut it won't turn. Rust: one, me: zero.":"3d158353c794","hero|There's a power junction box behind that fire. Label says 'POD FEED'.":"1dd4101a2e7c","hero|My bypass is holding. The pod bay has power.":"0fadcdb0191f","hero|The pod bay feed line is burnt clean through. I need a fresh length of cable to bridge it.":"2fa2b61acabe","hero|The power junction box for the pod bay. 'POD FEED'.":"849082f87082","hero|I can't get near it with that fire in the way.":"d6dde6bb5308","hero|Yikes. The pod feed line is completely burnt out.":"c90ee40881ec","hero|I'd need a fresh length of cable to bridge the gap.":"2f15857c54d1","hero|The bypass is working. Don't touch it. Don't even LOOK at it.":"e806bcc0e119","hero|I need something to bridge that burnt-out line.":"3985644d8cd1","hero|Okay. Bridging the gap... gloves on... annnnd...":"136d3a3e2dba","pa|POD BAY POWER: RESTORED.":"5f7d93abdfa6","hero|Ha! Still got it.":"bb161203a475","hero|It's not on fire. Well... not anymore.":"abe92f485c2f","hero|Hitting it won't help. Probably. Okay, it might feel good, but it won't help.":"0f316147f0ce","hero|A fire. On a spaceship. Right in front of the junction box. Of course.":"147664162cf9","hero|I'm not picking up a fire.":"44c3e8b3589f","hero|You don't use fire. Fire uses YOU.":"1b0f0fb0939b","hero|Please go out? ... No? Worth a shot.":"32fdcb9ccd54","hero|Stand back, fire!":"77ae4fa80094","hero|Fire: out.":"8f6e78bfb474","hero|Me: still flammable, but less so.":"e3f1d2ca1055","hero|Beat the fire with a stick? Very caveman. Very ineffective.":"49735fe463f0","hero|They're insulated against electricity, not against being on fire.":"ed8f2730bfba","hero|It's like an oven in here.":"1bc82254088c","hero|A really loud, really radioactive oven.":"7366f5973ffe","hero|Back to the corridor. No thanks.":"0e93f407b727","hero|Ares Prime. Rust-red, cold, and weirdly beautiful.":"8b7d498234ed","hero|Hopefully I'll see it up even closer. GENTLY.":"c8653952418e","hero|The only thing I'm opening is that pod.":"4b1036945014","hero|'LAUNCH TUBE 06. Dedicated to the crew of the ISV HALCYON.'":"50d40347df62","hero|'Lost, never forgotten. — Capt. Ines Vance, who flew her first.'":"98eb4950ddcd","hero|It's bolted on. And it clearly meant a lot to someone.":"fbea67701ed8","hero|The launch tube. The pod gets fired through there like a very expensive cork.":"3631819c5cdd","hero|Escape Pod 6. Seats one. Smells like new-pod smell and desperation.":"593c04dd6523","hero|It's a little big for my pockets.":"0d7c1bcc63d2","hero|The hatch is open. That seat looks SO comfy.":"df37616dae61","hero|The pod hatch. Sealed by the safety interlock.":"626df874e226","hero|The hatch is fine. It's the clamps that are stuck.":"8b84b9c7ce5d","hero|Released. Nothing's holding the pod back now.":"657af164ba77","hero|The launch clamps. Locked tight. They're supposed to release automatically. 'Supposed to.'":"7045a6327c2b","hero|They don't open by hand. There must be a release somewhere.":"2d3f42477434","hero|They're bolted to the deck.":"746c13e1e563","hero|I'd rather use the release lever than fight the clamps directly.":"31e042c74531","hero|Pulled, with a little help from my strut.":"9bc8c9e1a260","hero|The manual clamp release. Big red knob. Very pullable.":"37f23f6a4a4d","hero|Already pulled.":"e6d837cd0af6","hero|Nnnngh!":"79620a68c7d2","hero|It's jammed solid. I need more leverage.":"432783dcb4c1","hero|It's very firmly attached. Hence the problem.":"3e3d3c16b930","hero|It's a lever. You pull it. Or try to.":"5d189e1a4771","hero|Give me a lever long enough...":"7083270f4888","pa|LAUNCH CLAMPS DISENGAGED. POD 6 READY.":"801e2cd5211b","hero|Archimedes would be proud.":"49b39b26c6f1","hero|Better grip won't cut it. It needs LEVERAGE.":"d6342e8a236d","hero|There she is. Escape Pod 6.":"51dd45e7ad44","hero|My ticket off this flying scrapheap.":"4b82995f60ea","hero|Up the ladder. Back to where 'down' means something.":"abcf0ff48a30","hero|The ladder back up to the corridor. Up there, gravity still works.":"ec898684b5f6","hero|It's welded on. Good. At least one thing in here is staying put.":"65697b7491da","hero|The artificial gravity generator. Every single light on it says 'nope'.":"c89808b2b00d","hero|Unless I can fix gravity with harsh language, it's staying dead.":"b73815149116","hero|Its insides are slag.":"d14497bf8549","hero|Survey drones. Still strapped down. Never unpacked. Some survey mission.":"80f4766de6b4","hero|Container 7. 'Survey equipment.' Zero kilograms.":"77cbabd6f5ca","hero|The lines pulse slower when I stare at it. Like it's breathing.":"3762174971d0","hero|A huge black container. 'CONTAINER 7. DIRECTIVE 7.'":"2a9ba7e8c4f2","hero|Everything else in here is floating. It's just... hanging there. Perfectly still.":"55147e76a219","hero|I put my hand on it.":"1841cfe106e6","hero|It's warm. And it's humming. And for a second I swear...":"0e20ebe90d3f","hero|...it whispered my name.":"ea8680a48472","hero|No seams. No hinges. No lock. How did anyone put anything IN it?":"81b9a7329555","hero|It's the size of a truck. And it creeps me out.":"f6d5ea8f6169","hero|Uh... hello?":"db11c5d5167a","hero|The lines flickered. I'm choosing to believe that's a coincidence.":"e7e204a1ab46","hero|A wrench, drifting lazily. Someone didn't stow their tools.":"cefcca6c60dd","hero|Got it. In zero-g, everything's a free sample.":"8ebe64508d23","hero|The mission archive terminal. Still running on emergency power.":"122376edfd5d","hero|The cargo hold. Dark, cold, and... why is my stomach doing flips?":"b0a310f2a106","pa|WARNING: ARTIFICIAL GRAVITY FAILURE. CARGO DECK.":"06942dbe611f","hero|Oh no. No no no no—":"cb3b9cf3e717","hero|I lost my grip on the ladder, drifted out... and the air drag stopped me dead in the middle of the room.":"1f729d62ed64","hero|Nothing in reach. Nothing to push against. I'm a very confused balloon.":"86e258890939","hero|A gentle push...":"0ecbf18b1e5f","hero|...and the air drag slows me to a stop. Middle of the room. Again.":"2858f189e205","hero|I brace against the ladder and kick off!":"0885f308413e","hero|I plant my feet on the wall and push!":"e5fdba9147da","hero|Spraying straight at that won't get me anywhere useful.":"f69057ab122d","hero|Throwing it straight at that won't move me anywhere useful.":"7954e30b790f","hero|I'm already pressed against this side. Pushing harder would just squish me.":"680b208c3ae7","hero|FSSSSSHHH!":"7322b78c0800","hero|Heave!":"b61d6936c891","hero|Wait, WHAT? I went the WRONG way!":"b3ec37da4cf8","hero|...Oh. Right. Push stuff one way, I go the other. Newton's third law.":"e99b2148424e","hero|Thanks, Isaac. Very helpful. Eventually.":"c064847d097a","hero|Newton's third law: throw stuff one way, I go the other. Science!":"1c311c73fa02","hero|I flail. I wiggle. I go nowhere. No gravity, nothing to push against.":"79dd1146c237","hero|Swimming through air doesn't work. I've checked. Twice.":"42ecfa0d445d","hero|Push off toward what? I should pick a target.":"b31a294be1eb","hero|I can't walk. I can only drift.":"a01414d168ab","hero|It's out of reach. I'm floating in the middle of the hold with nothing to push against.":"f3b668fd421e","hero|Can't reach it. I need some way to move. Something to throw, maybe?":"dfe6e8852d6d","hero|I need to get over there first.":"4c88d092e508","hero|If I drift out to the middle with nothing to throw, I'll be stranded again. No thanks.":"7fe61d0b93ed","hero|It's already equalized.":"7ea48daebf85","hero|Hsssssssss...":"ae9d127557e6","hero|Air rushes from high pressure to low until both sides match. That hatch should open easily now.":"867909b6829e","hero|Hnnngh! It won't budge.":"778ce47b7329","hero|The hold has lost pressure, so all the air up here is pushing this hatch shut.":"1637a86a805b","hero|Point six atmospheres on a square-meter hatch... that's about six tonnes. I can't lift six tonnes.":"9812d92467b6","hero|Open. A ladder goes down into the cargo hold.":"eaa91f91bbc0","hero|'INSERT ID CARD.' Mine's back on my desk in my quarters.":"3e812d1e4d51","hero|Ines knew. She knew my name was coming out of that planet.":"f2934ebd94f8","hero|And Pod 6 is going to take me right to it.":"ed47d3290c1b","hero|...Great. Okay. Still better than exploding.":"03e156ac613a","hero|The yard office. Home of the Consortium's man on station: Rask.":"502d869656ac","hero|The Meridian, docked and gleaming. Half her bolts were torqued by yours truly.":"e79621c2bc8e","hero|And below us, the Moon's farside. The Consortium's had a dig site down there for decades. Nobody knows what for.":"eaaab060db10","hero|It's a window. Into space. Hard no.":"84b594aea6fe","hero|The yard coffee machine. Ninety-two degrees, every time. The most reliable machine on this station.":"17ee80a49a53","hero|I'm not voiding the warranty on the one thing that keeps this yard running.":"3228822ef859","hero|'ISV MERIDIAN. CREW: Vance, Okafor, Reyes, Brandt, Sato.'":"316c39a36b4c","hero|Five names. But the ship has six bunks and six escape pods.":"ed4b60f2fec2","hero|Somebody can't count. Or somebody isn't saying.":"f58c27a0bbeb","hero|The duty roster stays on the board. Union rules.":"f530632eecaf","hero|A real plant. On a space station. Somebody waters it every day. I've never seen who.":"51001be657eb","hero|The cargo dock. 'DIRECTIVE 7 PERSONNEL ONLY.' I've worked this yard two years and never heard of Directive 7.":"24ace23c3901","hero|Pry open a Consortium security door in front of everyone? Bold. Also: no.":"c8b2321738c4","hero|Pour coffee into a card reader? Tempting. Career-ending, but tempting.":"ad463f61775d","hero|Ines, giving Rask the full force of a captain's displeasure. Beautiful.":"1dc792c6c40f","hero|Captain Ines Vance. Twenty years flying, and she still watches her ship like it might leave without her.":"844645ec6bc3","hero|I offer her my coffee. She looks at it like it's evidence. Fair.":"1cc98c65b7c5","hero|She's a captain, not security. She doesn't care about my badge.":"807ee4bc58fe","hero|Rask, getting an earful from the captain. I could watch this all day.":"73dbd2f0624b","rask|Not now, Mr. Marlow. The captain is explaining arithmetic to me.":"6df5dde99f23","hero|I remember this place. The drydock. My last shift before... everything.":"29f23a99df80","hero|Right. A fault on the cargo crane. That was the job.":"7ece25b4495f","hero|I wave my badge at the reader...":"fa310c4dab5d","pa|CLEARANCE INSUFFICIENT.":"7ca2c7bd2260","hero|Figures.":"2dfbb21f6386","hero|One's enough. I'm jittery enough already.":"499da6d58a5c","hero|One coffee. Black. Scalding. Ninety-two degrees, says the display.":"d6235d82ab84","hero|Ines, sorry to—":"bc1aa06c7506","ines|Not now, Marlow. I'm busy being difficult.":"033d26e36374","ines|You must be the engineer yard ops sent up. Ines Vance. I'm captain of that beautiful thing out there.":"63d12a692ce9","hero|Kit Marlow, yard engineering. I'm here about a fault on the cargo crane.":"8179bec0ea31","ines|Good luck. Rask's people won't let anyone near the cargo dock. Not even me. On my own ship.":"674b864bb3ef","ines|Back again, Marlow?":"8e6378b518d3","hero|Tell me about the Meridian.":"2b5691a5f7bc","hero|What's in the cargo dock?":"dbc8476e8221","hero|Is that a Halcyon patch?":"091bcaeef145","hero|Can you get Rask out of his office?":"29e3552d0c8d","hero|See you later.":"ed7c9ab9b14e","ines|Survey ship. Six bunks, six pods, fourteen months to Ares Prime and back.":"e6ca614ab677","ines|Funny thing: they only gave me five crew. Nobody will tell me who bunk six is for.":"adbd4f46a934","ines|Container 7. 'Survey equipment.' Armed guards, a sealed manifest, and a Consortium minder named Rask.":"f7f714382f0a","ines|If you find out what's really in that box, I'd like to know before I fly it to another planet.":"7ab657b53725","ines|Good eye. The Halcyon. First ship I ever flew. We lost her on the Europa run.":"e05e167160ea","ines|I keep her name close. Plaques, passwords... you'd be amazed how often it comes in handy.":"b51b14aed2db","ines|Get Rask away from his desk? Marlow, I've wanted to yell at that man about the manifest all day.":"fedecfd66400","ines|Give me two minutes. And whatever you're up to, I didn't see it.":"0a04315a6f40","ines|Mind the gantries. And Marlow? Keep your head down around Rask.":"9968ad62a4c1","ines|Rask! A word. Now.":"b084d43afb32","rask|Captain. This had better be important. I was on with the Board.":"fa42cdf946ae","ines|Oh, it is. Let's go through your manifest. Line. By. Line.":"ec124684969b","hero|That's my cue. Rask's office is empty.":"13eba0bf227d","hero|Back out to the concourse.":"c830646097c6","hero|The lunar farside, close enough to touch. Somewhere down there is the Consortium's famous dig site.":"5225018790a4","hero|'A. Rask. Doctorate in Xenolinguistics.'":"52c6998aa9d7","hero|Xenolinguistics. The study of alien languages. For a SURVEY mission?":"37cc81c96f55","hero|Steal a man's diploma? Even Rask doesn't deserve that. Probably.":"6f3433d815f9","hero|A filing cabinet. Actual paper. The Consortium doesn't trust its own computers.":"4b9ce684d2f8","hero|Locked. Of course it's locked.":"440eecf65d0e","hero|The call's on hold. Just the Halvorsen-Arc logo, slowly turning.":"75666470bd49","hero|A holo-call with four silhouettes. The Halvorsen-Arc Board, I'd guess. None of them blink.":"7ef0e2c79055","hero|Hello, Board? ...Nobody's home. Good.":"bdda76f6e1a4","hero|I'm not interrupting the Board. I'd like to keep my job.":"f5353acb912a","hero|Rask's terminal. Still logged in. Sloppy, Rask.":"7f27b77a105f","hero|Rask's terminal. He's sitting right in front of it.":"36946945bf13","hero|The duct's open. The schematics say it runs straight into the cargo dock.":"147bb3c57466","hero|Maintenance duct 7-C. According to the yard schematics, it runs straight into the cargo dock.":"0caba4c8f667","hero|Not with Rask watching me like a hawk in a suit.":"8cc76d203ef6","hero|Nnngh! It won't budge. Any harder and I'll snap the bolt.":"28cc97113962","hero|The nut's seized onto the thread. If I could make the nut expand, just a little...":"8975fea829d1","hero|It's a duct, not a door. No card reader.":"9e221234a56a","hero|Rask. Consortium liaison. Expensive suit, cheap smile.":"49fead029e79","hero|I'd need a much bigger pocket. And a death wish.":"92ad92441582","hero|Throw coffee at Rask? Satisfying. Then I'd be fired AND out of coffee.":"6593aa8d0515","hero|Empty. And his terminal's still logged in.":"d353b24d3d29","rask|Yes? I'm on a call with the Board.":"3919e539b92e","hero|Kit Marlow, yard engineering. The cargo crane's load cell is reporting a fault. I need to inspect it.":"936a9e0572eb","rask|The load cell is functioning exactly as intended.":"663c082b7d45","hero|It reads zero kilograms. For a container the size of a truck.":"eceb4d6ad9ae","rask|Then it weighs zero kilograms. Is there anything else?":"cdbb3bb4888f","rask|You again.":"7ff2282808ac","hero|What's in Container 7?":"45a3dc810a32","hero|I need access to the cargo dock.":"98f3ce696c09","hero|Never mind.":"bb49406cfe67","rask|Survey equipment.":"c223c661afba","hero|Survey equipment doesn't usually need armed guards.":"289286b8fb3b","rask|It does when it's ours.":"5a857bb92a20","rask|Directive 7 personnel only. You are not Directive 7 personnel.":"5a2af2f20327","rask|...Yet.":"0649abea1d55","hero|Yet?":"b3f7adbfc209","rask|Good day, Mr. Marlow.":"47f55880a2a2","rask|Close the door on your way out.":"2de6457bc8ad","hero|I need him out of that office. Maybe the captain can help.":"1a247bffd12e","hero|Not while he's sitting right in front of it.":"79c54c27733f","hero|If that container reacts to me, I need to know why.":"fd881f8db586","hero|And I need to know before Rask does anything to my brain.":"e55578dfb347","hero|The retaining nut is seized solid. Tight threads, cold steel.":"cd2f36717091","hero|Hmm. I happen to be holding a very hot cup of coffee...":"e0e43e5c0ec3","hero|If I could make that nut expand, just a little, it'd break free.":"4502ab4b84d8","hero|Ninety-two-degree coffee, straight onto the nut.":"465fa108b4b3","hero|Heat makes metal expand. The whole nut grows outward, so the hole in the middle gets bigger too.":"9843a5400614","hero|Only by a few micrometres. But that's all it needs.":"14b5fd4b4cd3","hero|Multitool... and... it turns! Duct's open.":"9f7e54e16b04","hero|The duct back to Rask's office.":"86fd7b9d64ab","hero|The Meridian's cargo bay, wide open. Waiting to swallow whatever's in that box.":"385e65526f99","hero|The crane's load cell: zero point zero zero zero kilograms.":"b944f57be32e","hero|I tested that sensor twice this morning. It isn't faulty.":"aa9ca1102895","hero|That box really weighs nothing. Which is impossible. Things that big don't weigh nothing.":"18a8145a0f2f","hero|The routing panel for the alignment laser. Right now it's feeding the laser fence around the container.":"3a2a311afc6a","hero|A laser containment fence. Walk through that and I'll be sliced into a very thin engineer.":"51ce1dbc0c3a","hero|Absolutely not.":"815f0e5545b7","hero|I'd like to keep my fingers attached to my hand.":"c22acb22ae09","hero|Poke a laser with shiny metal? It'd just reflect it somewhere exciting.":"b0e5cf48ca1a","hero|Coffee doesn't stop lasers. I checked. Once. Long story.":"f9d973979450","hero|Container 7. The glyphs are brighter now. Brighter the closer I get.":"4b144c3e1006","hero|Container 7, behind the laser fence. Those lines on it... are they glowing brighter since I walked in?":"42fb915d8e3d","hero|It's the size of a truck. Weightless or not, it won't fit in my pocket.":"e26ae3ab1aa5","hero|No seams. No hinges. No lock.":"e4585536564f","hero|The dock's security door. Locked from Rask's side.":"426126b080fe","hero|The cargo dock. And there it is.":"a6885c6718ff","hero|Container 7. Why do I feel like it's... looking at me?":"2d813412e403","hero|The beam's going into the dump and the fence is down. I'm not touching it again.":"7b5981f21687","hero|Every mirror sits at forty-five degrees, so each one turns the beam through a right angle.":"afc99222103a","hero|Angle in equals angle out. I just have to steer the beam into the dump instead of the fence.":"67ebabbfe728","hero|Fence is down.":"6a76b449d9c9","hero|Not through the laser fence. I'd arrive in slices.":"894165d2facb","hero|Okay. Just a closer look. Nothing weird.":"291d1c546a88","hero|...It's warm. Why is it warm?":"ca1be1b39b78","it|KIT.":"a5867b8a1819","hero|Who said that?!":"cb085dc1079c","it|WE HAVE WAITED A LONG TIME FOR YOU TO HEAR US.":"42cef29c510a","it|THREE THOUSAND ONE HUNDRED AND SEVENTEEN YEARS.":"70fd33ab495a","it|COME TO US. LISTEN.":"fba7e8d8f048","rask|Step away from the container, Mr. Marlow.":"6a91951cc2df","hero|Rask! It... it TALKED to me!":"b187469e38eb","rask|Yes. It does that. To exactly one person.":"e9c6f642396d","rask|Board, this is Rask. Contact confirmed. Ninety-nine point seven percent.":"e2ca18462c51","rask|Initiate Directive Seven.":"a448de50ba39","ines|Rask! What are you doing to him?!":"35d2d7169291","rask|Saving your mission, Captain. Mr. Marlow has just volunteered.":"775e67312748","hero|Volunteered for WHAT?":"3f2cfa740d0e","ines|Kit... I'm so sorry.":"708aec37363d","hero|Pod 6. Scorched, dented, upside-down-ish... and it held.":"ded308d329e3","hero|Thanks, Ines.":"eb1400ea4e2e","hero|There's nothing left inside but a very sweaty seat.":"927ab04b26c3","hero|It's done flying. Forever.":"6cb6f56877bf","hero|The parachute. Martian wind is already trying to steal it.":"5fd2ee1af76c","hero|Footprints. Human. Fresh.":"c21a9191015f","hero|Leading straight toward that... thing.":"1ff64b711d12","hero|Somebody got here before me.":"0bdda510fb18","hero|Streaks of fire across the pink sky. The Meridian, coming down in pieces.":"313b2356a5aa","hero|A colossal black arch, half buried in the sand.":"381441452fc4","hero|Those lines on it. They're the same as Container 7's.":"88a8136ca9fa","hero|Ugh...":"5322d9b938d5","hero|I'm alive. The pod held.":"83976c43afb6","hero|And I remember. All of it. The container. Rask. Directive Seven.":"c6b3b9c4afac","hero|They didn't recruit me. They SHIPPED me. Like cargo.":"2eb94e3d72d2","hero|The same lines. The same light. The same feeling of being... watched.":"963922e37dd3","it|WELCOME HOME, KIT.":"88959f156098","hero|...Home?":"118e02f17059","pa|WARNING. HULL INTEGRITY CRITICAL. ALL PERSONNEL PROCEED TO ESCAPE PODS.":"cf4c48bf82ea","hero|Ugh... what hit me?":"aec4beb7b1de","hero|Oh. Right. The SHIP hit me.":"954a339b277e","pa|ORBITAL DECAY IN PROGRESS. ATMOSPHERIC BREAKUP IMMINENT.":"5baec50b6c60","hero|'Imminent.' Love that word. Very specific.":"055a37b89eca","hero|Okay, Kit. Get to the pod bay. How hard can it be?":"fc1e182c950c","hero|Gloves on. Steady... steady...":"987c2cd1cd3a","hero|GOTCHA!":"d92b39f13cf9","hero|I yanked it right out of the ceiling coupling. Now it's just a long, dead, very useful cable.":"376692e3fbd3","hero|I can't reach the panel with that cable thrashing around.":"0b3887236d35","hero|I swipe the card...":"490a67dc66b4","hero|Nothing. There's no power to the panel.":"56b79ce61b58","pa|ACCESS GRANTED. POD BAY OPEN.":"3bc4c1adce7b","hero|Finally, something on this ship that works.":"ef6711346ac6","hero|The hatch won't open. Safety interlock.":"410cabf80411","hero|The launch clamps are still engaged.":"587aec734459","hero|Hatch open. Let's get out of here.":"0948fef44ad2","hero|So long, Meridian. You were a terrible ship.":"4520a9d98b10","hero|I'll kind of miss you.":"1b739961ac4c","hero|Back in the pod.":"a3727246aef7","hero|A launch code. Of course there's a launch code.":"119c406a6a1f","hero|If anything on this ship knows it, it's the mission archive. That's down in the cargo hold.":"4cafaea6400b","hero|I need to pick the right burn. Think, Kit.":"b619e6457409","hero|Let's see what she's got...":"916f6214f70f","pa|POD BAY POWER: ONLINE (UNAUTHORIZED BYPASS DETECTED).":"89688577df27","pa|POD BAY POWER: OFFLINE. FEED LINE DAMAGED AT JUNCTION.":"7e585f481af7","pa|LAUNCH CLAMPS: DISENGAGED.":"9c3cb515a374","pa|LAUNCH CLAMPS: JAMMED. MANUAL RELEASE REQUIRED.":"b3174b7c17c5","hero|'Unauthorized.' Report me.":"1974f9372b1b","hero|Great. So that junction box is the problem.":"7d97ed7434d8","mabel|Engineering is on fire. Conveniently, there's an extinguisher in the case right next to you.":"f2e8ade95837","mabel|The case is locked, but it's only glass. Be creative.":"ba96dc0f2da1","mabel|Go put out that fire in Engineering before it spreads to... well, everything.":"39b83b2beae6","mabel|That loose power cable is blocking the pod bay. You'd need insulated gloves to handle it.":"3b8a011a49ec","mabel|Didn't you keep a pair in your locker?":"4be298de1d08","mabel|You have insulated gloves. Use them on that cable. Carefully. Please.":"459e03d14690","mabel|The pod bay's power feed is burnt out at the junction box in Engineering. Behind where the fire was.":"53444bad5dc1","mabel|That cable you're carrying would make a fine bypass.":"3d72f72dd072","mabel|Power's back. Swipe your ID card on the panel by the pod bay door.":"490ed4571d3b","mabel|Power's back. The door needs an ID card.":"c40615fa713b","mabel|Yours is on your desk. As usual.":"23b4e345b75b","mabel|The launch clamps tend to stick. Use the manual release lever in the pod bay.":"3819f5aeb3d2","mabel|If it's jammed, find some leverage. That strut, perhaps?":"6598a3a2211e","mabel|The pod is ready. Get in it, Kit. Now.":"5aae1739aeaf","mabel|The launch code will be in the mission archive, in the cargo hold under the corridor floor.":"698e258c30db","mabel|The hold lost pressure. Equalize it with the valve first, unless you enjoy arm-wrestling six tonnes of air.":"bccd442b0252","mabel|The archive terminal is in the cargo hold. Gravity's out down there.":"eb9bbab97999","mabel|If you get stuck floating: push something one way, and you go the other. Newton never fails.":"d21c62af2ef0","mabel|The archive needs your ID card. It's on your desk.":"e7949502c558","mabel|The captain's log is encrypted with her passphrase.":"6aa2ddb2d274","mabel|Ines was sentimental about her first ship. There's a plaque about it in the pod bay.":"4422a4f94365","mabel|You have the code. In the pod, the burn direction matters.":"e5904a6ecb68","mabel|To go down, slow down. Burn retrograde: against your direction of travel.":"d0d0e2bc34ae","hero|MABEL? You still online?":"b1cc1d9b4902","mabel|Barely. Forty percent of my processors are on fire, and the other sixty are panicking.":"178f65f82099","hero|MABEL, it's me again.":"6b1b8488c40a","mabel|I noticed. I have cameras. Some of them.":"0a58cc8c0c77","hero|What happened to the ship?":"ed4c254ab8d5","hero|How do I get off this ship?":"e1979265d4df","hero|Where is everyone?":"a22e8739581e","hero|What is Directive 7?":"de7176c7fa6f","hero|Will you be okay?":"18f23cac4c4f","hero|Gotta go.":"22489adffe9e","mabel|Officially? A micrometeoroid swarm. ...You've read the captain's log. You know it wasn't.":"ae0cd42e0757","mabel|Micrometeoroid swarm. It punched through six decks, the reactor shielding, and my favorite camera.":"28dbd17556e5","mabel|We're losing altitude. When we hit the atmosphere, the Meridian becomes confetti.":"3d2f6feed36b","mabel|The crew launched in pods one through five while you were unconscious.":"755e6c23753a","mabel|Pod six is yours. I told them you'd be fine. Please don't make me a liar.":"7b900e9c9752","mabel|Directive 7 is... a restricted order from the Halvorsen-Arc Consortium.":"91b604ac0bf3","mabel|I am not permitted to discuss it, Kit.":"fafcb7a7d57b","mabel|I am permitted to say that I'm sorry.":"d772f6bf375e","mabel|I go down with the ship. It's in my contract.":"b6d890551759","mabel|...It's not in my contract. I'm backed up on the planet relay. Go.":"04082a628936","mabel|Go. And Kit? Don't touch anything that sparks.":"ccb1516053d8","mabel|...So, everything. Don't touch everything.":"4356d0e37f65","hero|Those two don't go together.":"439f2cbba48b","hero|I can't combine those.":"9fd3ff1e9b23","hero|Nope. That makes nothing.":"5e1a5695020d","hero|I already have it.":"7f9c58bbc93c","hero|It doesn't open.":"f9a3224156f7","hero|Nothing special about it.":"d0e8e6d56e2d","hero|I can't pick that up.":"9de8992a6a58","hero|That's not coming with me.":"a966525b0ff4","hero|That doesn't open.":"76c9c52ac455","hero|There's nothing to open.":"54f7134cd289","hero|I can't use that.":"a237b40c4418","hero|How would that even work?":"1fc8a0928580","hero|It's not much of a talker.":"7951901c6bf6","hero|I'm not THAT lonely. Yet.":"68e35ff7e030","hero|That doesn't work.":"00faf02bfa19","hero|I don't think so.":"0cf071480684","hero|Nope. Wrong combination.":"893aed925fae","hero|That didn't sound good.":"f22c0ada1f61","hero|Hold together, old girl...":"69110921bd68","hero|Okay. Hurrying. Hurrying now.":"66141797a762","hero|I felt that one in my fillings.":"5bce65c39c8f","hero|Was that the reactor? Please don't be the reactor.":"278b6e21b594","hero|Faster, Kit. FASTER.":"f6b96dd18e84"}